Right now `Surgex.Changeset` only supports flat errors list. If the error occurs in a relation or embedded schema, it does not know how to translate it into a Jabbax document properly. This is quite limiting and this PR proposes a change to support nested errors.

Here's an example of a changeset with nested errors, used in tests:

```
#Ecto.Changeset<
  action: nil,
  changes: %{
    address: #Ecto.Changeset<
      action: :insert,
      changes: %{
        country: #Ecto.Changeset<
          action: :insert,
          changes: %{code: "es"},
          errors: [
            code: {"is invalid",
             [validation: :inclusion, enum: ["us", "ca", "pl"]]}
          ],
          data: #Surgex.ChangesetTest.TestSchema.TestAddress.TestCountry<>,
          valid?: false
        >,
        street: "Main"
      },
      errors: [city: {"can't be blank", [validation: :required]}],
      data: #Surgex.ChangesetTest.TestSchema.TestAddress<>,
      valid?: false
    >,
    name: "test"
  },
  errors: [],
  data: #Surgex.ChangesetTest.TestSchema<>,
  valid?: false
>
```

It becomes a Jabbax document looking like this:

```
%Jabbax.Document{
   errors: [
     %Jabbax.Document.Error{
       code: "required",
       source: %Jabbax.Document.ErrorSource{
         pointer: "/relationships/address/data/attributes/city"
       }
     },
     %Jabbax.Document.Error{
       code: "invalid_inclusion",
       source: %Jabbax.Document.ErrorSource{
         pointer: "/relationships/address/data/relationships/country/data/attributes/code"
       }
     }
   ]
 }
```

The code in the initial version is quite convoluted at some places, so any ideas to improve it would be greatly appreciated.
